| closed ring |\n| 4 | plus | 7×7 | 24 cells | closed ring |\n\nSo only shapes enclosed by a **complete rectangular ring** of 5 act as templates. Shapes sitting in an open, edge-assisted corner are decoys.\n\nThe corrected rule has three steps:\n1. Find colour-5 objects that are full rectangle rings. The test is that cell count = 2·(h+w)−4 and every cell lies on the bbox border.\n2. Every non-background, non-5, non-1 object inside such a ring's bbox is a template. Its key is its cropped mask, and its value is its colour.\n3. Any colour-1 object whose mask equals a template key is recoloured to that template's colour.\n\n**Applying it to the test**\n\n- The 5-objects of size 13 at [0,12,5,19] and [13,0,19,6] are open corners. That means the 2×3 block and the 4×4 rounded blob are *not* templates. The 1-coloured block at rows 2–3 and the blob at rows 8–11 stay 1.\n- The ring [13,12,19,18] has 24 cells, so it is closed. It encloses a colour-2 plus.\n- Therefore the two colour-1 pluses, at rows 9–11 x 1–3 and rows 9–11 x 14–16, become 2.\n- Everything else is unchanged.","code":"def transform(grid):\n    g = np.array(grid)\n    bg = background(g)\n    out = g.copy()\n    objs = objects(g, bg=bg)\n\n    def is_ring(o):\n        y0, x0, y1, x1 = o[\"box\"]\n        h, w = y1 - y0 + 1, x1 - x0 + 1\n        if h < 3 or w < 3 or o[\"size\"] != 2 * (h + w) - 4:\n            return False\n        return all(y in (y0, y1) or x in (x0, x1) for (y, x) in o[\"cells\"])\n\n    rings = [o[\"box\"] for o in objs if o[\"colour\"] == 5 and is_ring(o)]\n    templates = {}\n    for o in objs:\n        if o[\"colour\"] in (5, 1):\n            continue\n        oy0, ox0, oy1, ox1 = o[\"box\"]\n        for (y0, x0, y1, x1) in rings:\n            if y0 < oy0 and oy1 < y1 and x0 < ox0 and ox1 < x1:\n                key = tuple(map(tuple, (o[\"grid\"] != bg).astype(int)))\n                templates[key] = o[\"colour\"]\n    for o in objs:\n        if o[\"colour\"] == 1:\n            key = tuple(map(tuple, (o[\"grid\"] != bg).astype(int)))\n            if key in templates:\n                c = templates[key]\n                for (y, x) in o[\"cells\"]:\n                    out[y, x] = c\n                emit(out, f\"Colour-1 object at box {o['box']} matches the template inside a closed frame; recolour it to {c}.\")\n    emit(out, \"All shapes matching a closed-frame template recoloured; final grid.\")\n    return out\n","candidate_tactics":{"recolour":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Any colour-1 object whose mask equals a template key is recoloured to that template's colour."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Colour-1 object at box (11, 10, 12, 12) matches the template inside a closed frame; recolour it to 2."},{"source":"verified program checkpoint","text":"Colour-1 object at box (16, 2, 17, 4) matches the template inside a closed frame; recolour it to 2."}],"template":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The first attempt treated every non-1, non-5 shape as a template."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In pair 1, the vertical 1×3 bar of 2s was wrongly treated as a template."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"In pair 3, the stem-and-base shape of 3s was wrongly treated as a template."}],"topology":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"So only shapes enclosed by a **complete rectangular ring** of 5 act as templates."},{"source":"final explanation","text":"It encloses a colour-2 plus."}],"count":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"The test is that cell count = 2·(h+w)−4 and every cell lies on the bbox border."}],"crop":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Its key is its cropped mask, and its value is its colour."}],"layers":[{"source":"final explanation","text":"Find colour-5 objects that are full rectangle rings."}]},"provenance":{"reference_assisted":false,"query_labels_used_for_rule_diagnosis":false},"artifact_sha256":"9718002b24eb99bca24c92e87364cef4fca529203f7be747e4691879f8d89a5e","task_sha256":"46663b7cdf8f980